{"name":"Clairvoyance","hex":"#838493","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clairvoyance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The power to see or perceive things, objects or events beyond the natural range of the senses, such as the past or the future.","Acute intuitive insight or perceptiveness; sagacity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clairvoyance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clairvoyance","blocks":[{"text":"Clairvoyance is the claimed ability to acquire information that would be considered impossible to get through scientifically proven sensations, thus classified as extrasensory perception, or \"sixth sense\". Any person who is claimed to have such ability is said to be a clairvoyant."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Paul_Sedir_-_Les_Miroirs_Magiques_-_1907_p22_Clairvoyance.gif/330px-Paul_Sedir_-_Les_Miroirs_Magiques_-_1907_p22_Clairvoyance.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clairvoyance","wikidata":"Q2975244"},{"title":"Clairvoyance (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Clairvoyance is the 1986 debut studio album by the alternative rock band Screaming Trees, produced by Steve Fisk. Released on Velvetone Records, the album helped the band earn a contract with SST Records. While it is very much a combination of psychedelic and garage rock, it bears many similarities to early grunge. It was original limited to a pressing of 2,500 copies, which included full size, double sided inserts. In January 2005, it was re-issued on CD by Hall of Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Clairvoyance_%28Screaming_Trees_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clairvoyance_(album)","wikidata":"Q927989"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Character_reader_and_Clairvoyan